1=\"8\" x2=\"610\" y1=\"225.0\" y2=\"225.0\" stroke=\"#6B6152\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"616\" y=\"229.0\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#6B6152\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">$439.80</tspan> 200-day avg</text><circle cx=\"515.1\" cy=\"103.4\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#C9A84C\" stroke=\"#20242C\" stroke-width=\"1\"/></svg></figure>\n<p>These lines are mine, not yours: the 52-week high, the 50-day and 200-day averages, and my retracement of the June 25 low ($348.54) to the Nov 4 high ($559.15).</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Trend:</strong> up. Price $521.12 is above the 50-day ($518.20) and far above the 200-day ($439.80), but it slipped under the 20-day ($530.47).</li><li><strong>Momentum:</strong> RSI 47.7, neutral. Three lower closes since $545.18 on Nov 9.</li><li><strong>Ceiling:</strong> $559.15, the record high set Nov 4. The October high of $551.15 is the first hurdle.</li><li><strong>Floor:</strong> the 50-day at $518.20, then the Nov 2 low at $504.96. Under that, my 38.2% line at $478.70 and the September low at $486.00.</li><li><strong>Your tested edge:</strong> the uptrend half is true (price and 50-day above the 200-day). RSI is 47.7, not under 40, so the setup is not on. It would take a deeper dip.</li><li><strong>Scorecard:</strong> no open or watching play.</li><li><strong>Verdict:</strong> the chart supports the upside, weakly. It agrees with what management described (growth speeding up), but the stock is sitting right on its 50-day. A close below $504.96 would flip the lean to down; a close above $559.15 would confirm the up-move.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"what-would-change-this-read\">What would change this read</h3>\n<ul><li>The next report (date not found, likely late January): Azure against the 49–50% guide, cloud margin against 65%, and whether the backlog grows from $677B.</li><li>Nvidia on Nov 17 and Oracle around Dec 14: both speak to whether chips and buildings are arriving on time.</li><li>Any new word on OpenAI's cloud choices or its Azure commitment.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"confidence-and-sources\">Confidence and sources</h3>\n<p>Solid: results, guidance and balance sheet (10-Q and call transcript). Thin: Microsoft's own press release was not opened; total capital spending including leases rests on a recap; the next report date and FY27 spending were not found. Governance facts come from the FY2026 proxy and press reports opened Nov 12.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0000789019/000119312526436133/msft-20260930.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">10-Q</a> · <a href=\"https://www.webull.com/news/15828153888932864\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">call transcript</a> · <a href=\"https://www.constellationr.com/insights/news/microsoft-delivers-strong-q3-azure-growth-48\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Constellation Research</a> · <a href=\"https://www.neoteo.com/en/microsoft-reports-azure-capacity-delays-as-demand-outpaces-supply\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Neoteo recap</a> · <a href=\"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0000789019/000119312526427849/d61756ddef14a1.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FY2026 proxy</a> · <a href=\"https://www.directionsonmicrosoft.com/microsoft-openai-amend-their-agreement-again/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Directions on Microsoft, OpenAI amendment</a> · <a href=\"https://www.dealstreetasia.com/stories/openai-microsoft-agree-on-38b-revenue-sharing-cap-481952/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">DealStreetAsia, revenue-share cap</a> · <a href=\"https://www.trendforce.com/presscenter/news/20260930-13258.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TrendForce, Sept 30</a> · <a href=\"https://www.geekwire.com/2026/microsoft-evp-rajesh-jha-retiring-after-35-years-in-latest-exit-from-senior-leadership-team/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GeekWire</a> · <a href=\"https://fortune.com/2026/09/11/microsoft-head-of-communications-frank-shaw-leaving-after-nearly-30-years-of-shaping-the-software-giants-publ